Say when a recursive acquisition is taken, throttled

IOCoreSurfaceRoot is entered twice by the same thread and the second entry never
prints SM locked, so it is worth knowing whether the recursion branch is even
reached; if it is, the count is the only thing that changed. Printed on every hit
this line repeats dozens of times per nub and pushes the heartbeat, the match
return and every later marker off the visible tail, so only the first eight and
every 512th hit are kept, each carrying the running total.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -1846,6 +1846,14 @@ restart_sleep:                  wait_result = assert_wait( element,
 		} else { // it is the same thread, recursive access is allowed
 			// add one level of recursion
 			active->count++;
+			{
+				static unsigned long nio_rec_total = 0;
+				nio_rec_total++;
+				if (nio_rec_total <= 8 || 0 == (nio_rec_total % 512)) {
+					printf("\nnio: SM rec c=%d n=%lu t=%p",
+					    (int)active->count, nio_rec_total, current_thread());
+				}
+			}
 
 			// return unused queue element to queue
 			action = kPutOnFreeQueue;
